            <ArticleTitle>[T wave pseudo-normalisation during exercise test as a marker of significant ischaemia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>394-6; discussion 397</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a 50 year-old woman with unstable angina is presented. During the exercise test performed at 5th day of hospitalisation T wave normalisation in leads III, aVF, V4-V6 was observed. The subsequent angiography revealed critical stenosis of the right coronary artery and percutaneous coronary intervention was performed. Following intervention there were no T wave changes during exercise.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
